{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1539042-fairy-trods-giant-s-causeway","id":1539042,"title":"Fairy trods - Giant's Causeway","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-22T10:49:42-07:00","id":1539042,"title":"Fairy trods - Giant's Causeway","content":"Hello guys,<br /> <br /> I'm trying to integrate some fairy stuff in my game of werewolf happening in Scotland and Ireland. I'm planning to use the Giant's Causeway as a Trod going between Scotland and Ireland like in the myth of the place. Staffa island would be the other side, and in my head I wanted to make it a place related to the fae/changeling, one way or another.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering, first, can a non-faerie character normally open a trod ? I can just decide they can, but I've been wondering for a while.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, each trod as a very specific way to be opened. How would you design the opening of this one ? I've been looking for something that would somehow relate to the legend, like maybe someone of a certain size (to reflect the Giant's) should stand on a those special rocks struck by the waves while delivering a challenge speech, facing the direction of Scotland ?<br /> And Should it be the same on the other side ? Or could it be more something related to music (staffa Island grotto are supposed to be quite musicals ?)<br /> <br /> Also, the island is quite remote, so what could it be to changelings, and how would they use it ? If I'm not mistaken, it would be in the Tuath of Shadow in the kingdom of Dalriada ? It could perfectly be a forgotten site in the current times, especially since it's in the highlands and from what I read it's a bit, but I want my player to feel it's 'exotic' to them. If the pc found it, it could become something the fairy would like to get their hands back on, and negotiate with the players, for example.<br /> <br /> Did any of you already used those places in your own games ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8944,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","user":"Tanakyelle","date":". 07-23-2024, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T20:15:27-07:00","id":1539077,"title":"","content":"I think as written the answer is &quot;no&quot;. The only rules I remember mention the Wayfare Art. However, that is not how I run it in my chronicles (which in all honesty is for Werewolf).<br /> <br /> First, there are mentions of the Paths of Balor which are Trods that lead to the different Umbras. They are not full explained, but I always took it that the Green Paths of Balor (which lead to the Middle Umbra) were equivalent to the Trod domains mentioned in Werewolf. Since Garou can enter Trods (the domain), then they can enter the Dreaming from them provided they pass certain tests or challenges along the way. Typically only packs under Stag would ever do so.<br /> <br /> Second, there are just too many legends and folktales of ordinary humans stumbling into the Otherworld where the fairies live. Since I want my chronicles to roughly simulate that, I want the rules to allow that as well. The difference is that humans (or whoever) can only access trods at the specific times and places when such things are possible. These could be special times of the year (only on the summer solstice for example), only during specific liminal times or places (dawn, dusk, shores, cave entrances, etc.), require certain actions (which mortals might be able to espouse), or some combination of them. It is at these times that <i>some</i> Trods are naturally opened and anyway can travel between worlds. The mechanics of opening trods using Wayfare is just a special ability all Changelings could develop and can use at any time or place.<br /> <br /> For these kinds of trods that naturally open, I use actual folktales and legends to help me determine the circumstances and locations of such things. These trods are much a smaller subunit of all trods in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T13:06:45-07:00","id":1539110,"title":"","content":"I don't have my book here right now, so I can't say for sure the rules allow anyone to open a Trod, but I run things like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> suggested, and I do run Changeling more frequently than Werewolf.<br /> <br /> For the Causeway I think using personal size would be counterproductive and silly, but a challenge would be a fitting choice. Maybe shouting the challenge while branding an item that symbolize the giants, this one could be a giant version of something. Maybe a scepter made from a whole tree trunk that requires a Strength roll just to lift, and a Stamina roll to make the full challenge without letting it go.<br /> <br /> You can make the opening method from the other side as different as you want, the method is for the door, not the path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T10:23:35-07:00","id":1539226,"title":"","content":"I was thinking to do something along what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> is saying indeed in case it's normally changeling-restricted. Scotland is very rich in fairytales of all type, so I want to use it as much as I can. <br /> <br /> I love the idea of having an oversized object to symbolize the giants, I'll definitely use that. <br /> <br /> Thanks for all those info it's very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}